<title>AUSTRIA: One third of Vienna wurst-stands unhygienic.</title>
<headline>One third of Vienna wurst-stands unhygienic.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hygiene in more than 30 percent of kiosks selling popular wurst (sausage) in Vienna is below standard, Austria's Chamber of Labour said on Monday.</p>
<p>Tests showed a third of snack stands in the capital did not change the fat they used for frying sausages often enough, ruining the quality of the food, said the chamber, which looks after the interests of employees and consumers.</p>
<p>The fatty sausages and potato chips are a staple part of the Austrian diet and often the only fast food available late at night from the ubiquitous street stalls.</p>
</text>
